From 9e620286d55cfd8ffd4115df10a2aecfdaf84007 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: UMP <ump@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 53/90] Mods' content: overlay files linked and copied by
 several threads

Building a big pack's content overlay wrote its files one at a time: the base's ~23,000 links (copies where no hard link can be made: the game folder on another drive than the prepared files) and the mods' own files (over 150,000 for 184 mods). From a USB disk that took over 20 minutes after 'content mod(s) made', the window frozen. Both now run on several threads: link() collects the tree's files and links them in parallel; copy_plain_files() writes every mod file that is only copied (the last mod with a path owns it, as before), and the sequential pass reads only the files it parses.

UMP: 184 mods, first start on an SSD: ready in 895 s, world joined (it did not finish in 25 minutes before).
